30,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"It seems we are in a precarious position. We are losing key administrators, and the depot supervisors tend to ignore standard training in favor of their own routines.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"Oh man, the yards are a mess! We have a mix of old devices, and trying to switch systems during peak season is a total disaster.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The financial records are telling. Capital requests are being cut, but operating costs are slipping through. Bundled agreements are stable, but separate licenses climb every year.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"This is exactly what I feared. Last winter, no one took ownership of the outage, and our warehouse rules change too fast for any frozen project scope.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"My findings suggest a pattern of neglect and poor execution. We've skipped upgrades due to testing burdens, and external data migrations have left us with lasting errors.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Kenji, if the hardware is outdated and the supervisors resist training, any complex rollout will likely fail regardless of the software's features.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Misaki, you're right! We need something that can actually survive the yard and doesn't need a perfect schedule to work.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Yumi, the lack of ownership you found suggests that a fragmented support model is a liability. We should avoid systems with multiple separate licenses.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Toshio, I agree. If we have a ""finger-pointing"" situation during a crash, it doesn't matter how the bill looks. We need a single point of accountability.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, @Toshio, it seems we are all describing a systemic fragility. We need a solution that avoids external migration errors and doesn't require weeks of downtime for upgrades.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Yumi"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Misaki,,We must prioritize a vendor that provides heavy on-site support or training that actually sticks with the depot crews.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Kenji,,And it has to be something that doesn't break the depot during the November to January rush!,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Toshio,,I will be looking for a cost structure that is predictable. A fixed-price or bundled model is far safer than a modular one with climbing add-ons.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Yumi,,I want a vendor who takes full responsibility for the system and can handle a scope that evolves with the business.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"I shall favor a system that is robust enough to avoid the ""age in place"" trap and doesn't rely on external firms for critical data lifts.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
