55,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"Looking at the candidates, Anchor Industrial Software seems best. They have an engineering team present through rollout, which helps with our supervisor and staffing issues.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Kenji,,Anchor sounds great because it's built for transport operators! It's more likely to survive our yards than a general cloud suite.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Toshio,,I disagree with the modular approach of Corvus. Anchor's on-premise model with a dedicated team suggests more predictable long-term maintenance than climbing subscription add-ons.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"Meridian offers a fixed configuration and a regional team, which solves the ownership problem. But Anchor's on-site engineers might be better for the changing warehouse rules.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,Tessera's reliance on a partner firm for migration is a red flag given the 2018 pay move disaster. Anchor's internal engineering team is much more logical.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Yumi, Anchor's presence during rollout is exactly what we need to ensure the depot supervisors don't just drop the new routines.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, if Anchor is built for us, we won't have to ring it with spreadsheets like we did in 2021!","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Misaki, @Kenji, the stability of Anchor's deployment model aligns with the need to avoid the operating cost creep I found in the invoices.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Yumi,,I'm leaning toward Anchor too. Having the engineers there means we have someone to hold accountable when the plan stops matching the business.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,The logic is consistent. Anchor avoids the pitfalls of external partners and the fragility of modular licensing. It is the most robust choice.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Misaki,,I am satisfied. Anchor addresses the human resource gap and the training resistance. I vote for Anchor Industrial Software.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Kenji,,I'm all in! It's the only one that feels like it belongs in a real depot. I vote for Anchor Industrial Software!,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Toshio,,It minimizes the risk of hidden costs and support fragmentation. I vote for Anchor Industrial Software.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Yumi,,It provides the accountability and flexibility we've been missing. I vote for Anchor Industrial Software.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,It is the only candidate that avoids our historical patterns of failure. I vote for Anchor Industrial Software.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
